.TH MDT.NID_STATS_IDLE_TIME 4 2026-09-08 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.nid_stats_idle_time, obdfilter.nid_stats_idle_time \- per-NID idle timeout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME "*.nid_stats_idle_time"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME "*.nid_stats_idle_time=" TIMEOUT
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param obdfilter." FSNAME "*.nid_stats_idle_time"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param obdfilter." FSNAME "*.nid_stats_idle_time=" TIMEOUT
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT and OST device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present.
.TP
.B Default
.br
3600 seconds (1 hour)
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB nid_stats_idle_time= 0
.br
.RB nid_stats_idle_time= 2147483647
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B nid_stats_idle_time
parameter controls the amount of time in seconds that a per-NID statistic
structure associated with an export remains idle with no active exports or
connections before being automatically garbage collected. This prevents memory
and debugfs bloat in high-churn cloud environments where client virtual
machines are frequently created and destroyed.
.PP
Setting the value to
.B 0
disables the automatic garbage collection of idle NID statistics.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.nid_stats_idle_time
.B obdfilter.*.nid_stats_idle_time
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the NID stats idle timeout to 2 hours (7200 seconds) on the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB mgs# " lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.nid_stats_idle_time=7200"
.EE
.PP
Disable automatic garbage collection of idle NID statistics on all MDTs and
OSTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB mgs# " lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.nid_stats_idle_time=0"
.RB mgs# " lctl set_param -P obdfilter.testfs-*.nid_stats_idle_time=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B mdt.nid_stats_idle_time
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.57
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl (8)
